{%- comment -%}
  Shared markup is prepended to every view layout before rendering, so the
  assigns below are in scope for all four layouts.

  Polled responses (see settings.yml polling_url):
    IDX_0 = /users/me
    IDX_1 = the scope query, page_size 1, newest first — supplies open_total,
            and its item is the Next-up fallback when nothing has a due date
    IDX_2 = overdue count    (scope AND due_date <  today)
    IDX_3 = due-or-overdue   (scope AND due_date <= today)
    IDX_4 = soonest-due open item — the real Next up
    IDX_5 = closed-today count (status entered Done today; only pagination.total_items is read)
    IDX_6 = today's activity across all visible workspaces
    IDX_7/IDX_8 = next in-progress / planned milestone of the configured
            workspace (optional poll — both lines vanish when the milestone
            workspace ID field is blank)

  Accuracy note: every counter comes from pagination.total_items and is exact
  for any backlog size. due_today_count is derived as IDX_3 minus IDX_2, both
  server-side counts taken moments apart, so an item whose due date lands on
  today is counted correctly even with a backlog far larger than any window.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign me = IDX_0.data -%}
{%- assign open_total = IDX_1.pagination.total_items -%}
{%- assign overdue_count = IDX_2.pagination.total_items -%}
{%- assign due_today_count = IDX_3.pagination.total_items | minus: overdue_count -%}
{%- assign closed_today = IDX_5.pagination.total_items -%}
{%- assign activity = IDX_6.data -%}
{%- assign activity_total = IDX_6.pagination.total_items -%}

{%- comment -%}
  A failed poll yields {} rather than an exception, so an unreachable server
  or a rejected query would otherwise render as a silently blank screen. The
  device has no logs to check, so name the fault on the screen itself.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign fault = '' -%}
{%- unless me.id -%}
  {%- assign fault = 'Cannot reach Windshift. Check the server URL and API token.' -%}
{%- endunless -%}
{%- if fault == '' -%}
  {%- unless IDX_1.pagination and IDX_2.pagination and IDX_3.pagination and IDX_4.pagination -%}
    {%- assign fault = 'Windshift rejected the scope query. Check the QL syntax.' -%}
  {%- endunless -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Next up is the soonest-due open item that is not overdue (IDX_4, server-side
  sort by due date ascending, overdue already excluded by the query). With no
  due dates anywhere, fall back to the most recently touched item so the
  "Next up" slot still says something useful.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign next_up = IDX_4.data.first -%}
{%- unless next_up -%}{%- assign next_up = IDX_1.data.first -%}{%- endunless -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Next milestone is the first in-progress or planned milestone in the
  configured workspace's manual ordering, whichever sorts first. The poll is
  optional, so a blank field or a failed request just hides the row.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign next_milestone = IDX_7.data.first -%}
{%- if IDX_8.data.first and IDX_8.data.first.position < next_milestone.position -%}
  {%- assign next_milestone = IDX_8.data.first -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- unless next_milestone -%}{%- assign next_milestone = IDX_8.data.first -%}{%- endunless -%}

{%- assign owner_name = me.first_name -%}
{%- if owner_name == blank -%}{%- assign owner_name = me.full_name | split: ' ' | first -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if owner_name == blank -%}{%- assign owner_name = me.username -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} Centred message, used for the fault state. {%- endcomment -%}
{% template notice %}
  <div class="layout layout--col layout--center">
    <span class="value value--small">{{ headline }}</span>
    <span class="label">{{ detail }}</span>
  </div>
{% endtemplate %}

{%- comment -%} One stat tile. {% render %} is scope-isolated, so pass everything in. {%- endcomment -%}
{% template stat %}
  <div class="item">
    <div class="content">
      <span class="value value--{{ size | default: 'base' }} value--tnums">{{ number }}</span>
      <span class="label label--small">{{ caption }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endtemplate %}
